<title>EGYPT: Egypt crude, natgas output falls again in June.</title>
<headline>Egypt crude, natgas output falls again in June.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian crude oil production fell for the fourth consecutive month in June to an average of 830,000 barrels per day (bpd) from 836,452 bpd in May, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>EGPC said natural gas output also fell, to 1.173 billion cubic feet a day from 1.319 billion cubic feet in May.</p>
<p>Condensates were lower in June at 39,100 bpd compared to 39,323 bpd and butane and propane output fell to 30,000 bpd from 31,580 bpd in May.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
